                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "EDIT: Could not beat level 7, wave 1. On PS4 the wave had mines, which would help extend the timer, but not on PC apparently.\n\nGood music, but spends too much time playing mellow music and changes tracks at random intervals. Would be better to change tracks with spawns or even just when a new wave starts.\n\nStarts off easy, but from level 4 some game sense is needed. Enemy placement seems deliberate and encourages tactics to get rid of them efficiently.\n\nEnemy variety is excellent and they appear distinct so you can know which enemy type it is at a glance. The yellow and orange small fry blurs together in a pinch though.\n\nI found upgrades to be unbalanced but at least many are cool to try. The extra time/health upgrades seems mandatory sometimes, so I just left them on. And upgrading shooting seems cool at first, but you often get surrounded, so I felt like I needed AoE - when I have AoE, shooting seems secondary and a waste of upgrades. You get a secondary weapon which buffs shooting a lot, so maybe with that one, or if you got bullet hell skills, you may have more build variety.\n\nSome times I could not fire special weapons (explosions, mines). Never found out why. Seems like they are limited, but most of the time I could fire as many as I wanted. Maybe when low on health?\n\nVery frustrating that you can accidentally move into a spawning enemy, because they spawn with so little warning.\n\nAs a casual player, I disliked how some upgrades was locked behind scoring challenges as a result. Felt like a certain achievement was out of my reach. Leaderboards and scores are not really my thing, so I'm biased.\n\nText introducing new enemies are shown without pause while the new enemies spawn, which was frustrating. Took me some time to discover the stealth mechanic. Maybe I missed it in some text while I was under attack?",
